{#- Shared shell for every /admin/ page.

    DELIBERATELY DOES NOT LOOK LIKE /staff/. The two areas answer different
    questions — "my work" versus "everyone's accounts" — and a person who
    cannot tell at a glance which one they are in will eventually do something
    org-wide while believing it was local to them.

    The difference is carried by three things at once, so it survives being
    seen in a hurry, in grayscale, or by someone who does not notice color:
    the wordmark says ADMINISTRATION, the accent is amber rather than blue,
    and a stripe runs the full width above the header.

    AUTH: Access gates /admin* at the edge exactly as it gates /staff*, so the
    visitor is authenticated by the time this renders. That is NOT the same as
    being permitted: /api/admin refuses anyone without the admin role, and
    these pages show an explanation rather than data when it does. Markup is
    not a permission. -#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
<title>{{ adminTitle }} · Thauma Administration</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/tokens.css?v={{ "/css/tokens.css" | v }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/staff.css?v={{ "/css/staff.css" | v }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/admin.css?v={{ "/css/admin.css" | v }}">
{% set consoleApp = true %}{% include "brand-head.njk" %}
{% include "console-roles-head.njk" %}
</head>
<body class="is-admin" data-admin-page="{{ adminPage }}">

{#- The stripe. Full width, above everything, present on every admin page and
   on none of the staff ones. -#}
<div class="admin-stripe" aria-hidden="true"></div>

{% include "console-header.njk" %}

<main>
  <div class="page-head">
    {#- The page's name, without a number: the numbers disagreed with each
       other (two 04s, two 05s) and so meant nothing (mockup board 1). -#}
    {%- if areaTab %}
    <div class="cue"><span data-i18n="adm.nav.{{ adminPage }}">{{ areaLabel }}</span></div>
    {%- else %}
    <div class="cue"><span data-i18n="adm.page.{{ adminPage }}.title">{{ adminTitle }}</span></div>
    {%- endif %}
    <div class="sec-h">
      <h1 id="pageHeading" data-i18n-html="adm.page.{{ adminPage }}.heading">{{ adminHeading | safe }}</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  {#- Shown when the endpoint refuses. The pages are reachable by anyone Access
     lets through; the DATA is not, and this is what that looks like. -#}
  <p class="rolegate" id="notAdmin" hidden>
    <b>You are signed in, but this area is limited to administrators.</b>
    Your account can use the <a href="/staff/">staff console</a>.
  </p>

  {%- if areaTab %}
  {#- AN AREA OF THE PUBLIC SITE'S WORK (consoleNav.js `areas`): its tabs —
     down the left on Site Creator, as the staff one has them, or across
     the top — then the tab on screen, and on Site Creator the page as it
     will look beside it (admin.css AREAS). Updates and Site Creator have
     the publish bar and review along the foot. -#}
  {%- set area = consoleNav.areas[adminPage] %}
  <div class="web{% if area.side %} is-side{% endif %}" id="webArea" data-area="{{ adminPage }}" data-tab="{{ areaTab }}">
    {%- if area.tabs.length > 1 %}
    <nav class="web-side" aria-label="{{ adminTitle }}">
      {%- for t in area.tabs %}
      <a href="{{ t.url }}" data-web-tab="{{ t.tab }}"
         {% if t.tab == areaTab %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
         data-i18n="web.{{ t.tab }}">{{ t.label }}</a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </nav>
    {%- endif %}
    <div class="web-main">
      {{ content | safe }}
    </div>
    {%- if adminPage == "website" %}{% include "website/preview.njk" %}{% endif %}
  </div>
  {%- if area.publish %}{% include "website-publish.njk" %}{% endif %}
  {%- else %}
  {{ content | safe }}
  {%- endif %}
</main>

<script src="/js/staff-i18n.js?v={{ "/js/staff-i18n.js" | v }}"></script>
<script src="/js/staff.js?v={{ "/js/staff.js" | v }}"></script>
<script src="/js/console-app.js?v={{ "/js/console-app.js" | v }}"></script>
<script src="/js/console-translate.js?v={{ "/js/console-translate.js" | v }}"></script>
{#- Before admin.js, which calls it the moment somebody picks a file; the
   cropper opens the one photo editor, so that comes first. -#}
<script src="/js/photo-editor.js?v={{ "/js/photo-editor.js" | v }}"></script>
<script src="/js/photo-crop.js?v={{ "/js/photo-crop.js" | v }}"></script>
<script src="/js/rich-text.js?v={{ "/js/rich-text.js" | v }}"></script>
<script src="/js/site-rich.js?v={{ "/js/site-rich.js" | v }}"></script>
<script src="/js/admin.js?v={{ "/js/admin.js" | v }}"></script>
{#- Page-specific behavior, loaded only where it is used. admin.js is the
   shared shell — identity, the role gate, the pages that read /api/admin.
   Content and Site talk to a different endpoint and have nothing in common
   with it beyond the layout. -#}
{#- Hashed here, not in the page's front matter: front matter cannot run a
   filter, so a version written there is a hand-maintained number — the exact
   thing the content hash exists to remove. -#}
{%- if adminScript %}<script src="{{ adminScript }}?v={{ adminScript | v }}"></script>{% endif %}
{#- Publishing, and the data-mover inside its review, on every Website screen
   and nowhere else. -#}
{#- AN AREA IS ONE PAGE: each of its tabs' scripts, so every tab loads at
   once, then the shell that moves between them (admin-website.js). Only
   the area's own — Site Creator does not wait for the mail. -#}
{% if areaTab %}{% for f in consoleNav.areas[adminPage].scripts %}
<script src="/js/{{ f }}.js?v={{ ("/js/" + f + ".js") | v }}"></script>{% endfor %}
{%- if adminPage == "mail" %}
{#- Thauma's Mail writes with the same composer as the staff Mail page,
   after staff-mailing.js, which it reads (see staff.njk). -#}
<script defer src="/js/composer.bundle.js?v={{ "/js/composer.bundle.js" | v }}"></script>{% endif %}{% endif %}
</body>
</html>
